    {
      "id": "gate",
      "page": "foundations",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -250,
      "w": 980,
      "text": "PETROL + CONSOLE. This is the binding handoff for tokens.css - nothing in src/ gets written until it is approved.\n\nThe one conflict the form study left open is resolved here: display rows sit at 40 px, but any row holding a control is 52 px so the control keeps its full 44 px target. Density where it is free, never at the cost of the floor.\n\nEvery contrast number on these artboards is computed by tools/palette-report.mjs. All 27 pairs pass in both appearances; the tightest is the decorative hairline at 1.32.",
      "kind": "note"
    },
    {
      "id": "formpick",
      "page": "form",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Settled: CONSOLE.\n\nKept as the record of what was compared. All three dropped the card-in-a-card habit; Console won because the row - not the box - became the unit, which is what the density is actually for."
    },
    {
      "id": "pick",
      "page": "directions",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Settled: PETROL.\n\nKept as the record. Each candidate changed hue, chroma, form and type together, and all 27 contrast pairs pass in both appearances for every one of them - so the choice was about character, not about which one was safe."
    }
  ],
